# llm_note = AICTP frame. "according to our record" = parenthetical obl. "we know our record to be true" = parenthetical advcl (evaluative). "behold" = INTJ discourse. Existential: "it was a just man" (identificational copula). "who did keep the record" = relcl, "did" = emphatic AUX. Dash = punct attached to record (word 34). "for he truly did many miracles" = new clause: "did" as auxiliary to a zero main verb (or bare "do": he did [do] many miracles) — treat as emphatic: he=nsubj, did=AUX, many miracles=obj, main verb elided; attach obj to "did" and treat did as VERB here (alternative: treat as "he did [do]" with elided V). Best: "he truly did many miracles" — did=VERB (past tense of "do" meaning "performed"), miracles=obj. Second "there was not any man" = negative existential. "save he were cleansed" = conditional exception: save=SCONJ.
